}
```

### Expected Result

The rule should report `if (value)` with `Expected non-Promise value in a boolean conditional.`, as it already does for `number | Promise<number>`.

With `flagUnions: "strict"`, the same should apply to `number | string | Promise<number> | Promise<string>`, since the awaited types of the Promise constituents exactly match the non-Promise constituents.

### Actual Result

No error is reported for `if (value)` when `value` has the type `number | string | Promise<number> | Promise<string>`.

In contrast, changing the type to `number | Promise<number>` while keeping the same `flagUnions: "strict"` setup correctly reports `Expected non-Promise value in a boolean conditional.`

### Additional Info

`hasMatchingPromiseTypeArgument` uses `.find()` to select a single Promise-like constituent.

When the union contains multiple Promise constituents, the remaining ones are treated as non-Promise constituents, causing the comparison to return `false`.

